// York Standard Library - std/mem/arena.yk
// Documentation & guidelines for York native Arena allocations.
//
// Arena<T> is York's zero-fragmentation, contiguous memory buffer.
// Built-in methods available on any Arena<T>:
//   .push(item)       - append element, auto-growing buffer if needed
//   .get(index)       - fetch element at index
//   .set(index, item) - overwrite element at index
//   .pop()            - remove and return the last element
//   .last()           - peek at the last element
//   .clear()          - reset count to 0 without reallocating
//   .count()          - current number of elements
//   .is_empty()       - true if count == 0
//
// Example:
//   Arena<int> nums = new Arena(16);
//   nums.push(42);
//   nums.set(0, 100);
//   int val = nums.get(0);
//   int popped = nums.pop();
//   bool empty = nums.is_empty();
